  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Open Ledger",
    "overview": "The app is an open ledger: flat pages, plain rows, every entry legible at a glance. It exists to show a reviewer that a small auth flow was built deliberately, so the interface carries the same candour as the documented decisions behind it. Nothing is staged. A screen states what happened and what to do, then stops.\n\nThe voice is calm, direct and trustworthy. One narrow column of content sits on a quiet tinted page. Hierarchy comes from size, weight and spacing, never from decoration. A single blue marks the one thing you can act on, and the rest is ink on paper.\n\nIt rejects three things, all confirmed: the glossy SaaS look (gradients, glows, floating shadowed cards, big hero sections), the default auth-template look (a form centred on a grey backdrop, an invented logo, \"Welcome back\" copy), and the colourful-shop look (several accent colours, badges, promo banners). The system is meant to grow into a shop without becoming any of these.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Flat: depth comes from a tinted page, a white surface and a 1px rule, never from shadow.",
      "One accent, used for actions and focus only.",
      "One typeface, hierarchy by weight and size.",
      "A single 384px column, generous top and bottom space.",
      "Light and dark follow the system setting; both are first-class."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Voice Rule",
        "body": "Ledger Blue is the only accent. It marks what can be acted on and where focus is. If something is blue, it is interactive.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Red Is For Errors Rule",
        "body": "Alert Red appears only when something went wrong. It is never used for emphasis, sale tags or decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Control Boundary Rule",
        "body": "A control's edge must reach 3:1 against what it sits on (WCAG 1.4.11). Decorative hairlines stay faint; anything the User types into uses Field Rule.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tinted Neutral Rule",
        "body": "Neutrals carry a trace of the accent's hue (255 to 260). Never use pure grey or pure black for text or borders; pure white is reserved for the Page surface.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Family Rule",
        "body": "Geist only. Hierarchy comes from weight (400, 500, 600) and size, not from adding a second face.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Quiet Heading Rule",
        "body": "One headline per page, semibold, never above 1.5rem in this column layout. A heading announces the page, it does not perform.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Column Rule",
        "body": "Forms and detail views live in the 384px column. Do not widen it to fill the screen.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat-By-Default Rule",
        "body": "Surfaces are flat at rest. Separate them with tone and a 1px Rule, never with a shadow. If an overlay (menu, dialog) is added later, it may take one very soft shadow, and that decision belongs in this file first.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Radius Rule",
        "body": "6px everywhere. Do not introduce a second radius for emphasis.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep Ledger Blue for actions and focus only (The One Voice Rule).",
      "**Do** separate surfaces with the Page/Paper tone difference and a 1px Rule, and outline inputs with Field Rule so their edges meet 3:1.",
      "**Do** use 6px radius on everything, and 150ms colour-only transitions for state changes.",
      "**Do** keep a visible 2px focus outline on every interactive element, and announce errors with `role=\"alert\"`.",
      "**Do** use the glossary's words in copy: User, Registration, Login.",
      "**Do** design the dark theme alongside the light one; both follow the system setting."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use the glossy SaaS look: no gradients, glows, glass, floating shadowed cards or oversized hero headings.",
      "**Don't** use the default auth-template look: no form floating on a grey backdrop, no invented logo or brand mark, no \"Welcome back\" copy.",
      "**Don't** make it a colourful shop: no second accent colour, no badges, no promo banners, no decorative red.",
      "**Don't** add a second typeface or a second radius.",
      "**Don't** use pure grey or pure black for text or borders.",
      "**Don't** say which field was wrong on a failed Login.",
      "**Don't** use the words Account, Member, Customer, Sign-up or Sign-in in the interface."
    ]
  }
}
